Z||000000||MEC91Firebird||02-01-2001||12:20 AM||||Why should Ferarri 360 drivers be among the few lucky individuals who get to see there engines in the rear view mirror when they drive?  Shouldnt we all be so lucky?  Anyone ever thought of cutting a square out of the engine hatch and replacing it with glass or some heat resistance clear plastic? If the rear end of the glass was elevated, it might give better engine ventalation?.  I for one think this would be a very sharp mod, and it would be fun to look at the GM "Redhead" motor in the back!!||||reg||6
Z||000001||stimpy||02-01-2001||12:26 AM||||I'm with you on this one.  I know that I have seen pics of Japanese showcars with plexi inserts in the hoods to show off the engine. I'm sure it can be done. would be tough on notchy Fieros due to the hump, and I'd be afraid to hack up my GT's decklid. That shouldn't stop you though. Post pics when you are done.||||reg||1
Z||000002||MEC91Firebird||02-01-2001||12:36 AM||||I almost think the hump might be an aid of some sort, i havent done any measuaring, checking sketching yet, this is just my brainstorming session for this idea, i think if you cut out the hup, the end could be open the inch or so from the rest of the deck, like a sorta cowl induction/exauhst type thing.  I think my first "operation" will be on a junkyard car, then transfered to my lid, or have the junk lid  repainted, and put in my places, then i can go back to stock if its ever needed...  ||||reg||1
